.TH GETRLIMIT 2
.SH NAME
getrlimit, setrlimit \- read or change native process resource limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/resource.h>
.PP
.BI "int getrlimit(int " resource ", struct rlimit *" limit ");"
.br
.BI "int setrlimit(int " resource ", const struct rlimit *" limit ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Astia supports RLIMIT_NOFILE and RLIMIT_AS.  RLIMIT_NOFILE limits descriptor
numbers allocated by the process (the limit is one greater than the largest
allowed descriptor).  RLIMIT_AS limits the total bytes in the process VMA
accounting.  Limits are copied by fork and are not host-process limits.
.PP
The initial NOFILE hard and soft limit is 64.  The initial AS limit is
RLIM_INFINITY.  A process may lower either limit, but may not raise its hard
limit.  A new mapping exceeding RLIMIT_AS fails with ENOMEM and a descriptor
allocation exceeding RLIMIT_NOFILE fails with EMFILE.
.SH RETURN VALUE
These libc functions return zero on success, or -1 and set errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.B EFAULT
is returned for an inaccessible limit pointer.
.B EINVAL
is returned for an unsupported resource, invalid ordering, or a limit above
the native descriptor table size.
.B EPERM
is returned when a hard limit would be raised.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mmap (2),
.BR getrlimit (3),
.BR setrlimit (3)
